    {
      "beat_id": "BDEFS",
      "act": "DEFINITIONS",
      "lane": "CARD",
      "narration_text": "Five words before we start. SKILL dot m-d: a markdown file Claude Code loads on demand — zero cost until it's called. Frontmatter: the YAML block at the top; a name and a description. The description IS the trigger — the sentence that tells Claude when to auto-launch this skill. The Never section: rules the model tries to follow but isn't forced to. And definition of done: a script the skill runs after producing output — PASS or FAIL.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 28.1,
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "am_onyx",
      "new_visual_element": "CCDefinitions — five terms",
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "drawon",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "CCDefinitions",
          "props": {
            "title": "TERMS IN THIS FILM",
            "terms": [
              {
                "term": "SKILL.md",
                "meaning": "a markdown file Claude Code loads on demand — zero cost until called"
              },
              {
                "term": "frontmatter",
                "meaning": "the YAML at the top of SKILL.md — `name` and `description`"
              },
              {
                "term": "trigger sentence",
                "meaning": "the `description` — tells Claude when to auto-launch this skill"
              },
              {
                "term": "Never section",
                "meaning": "advisory rules the model tries to follow — not enforced by the harness"
